**Key idea:** The virtual interface is set in the **top-level module's `initial` block before `run_test()`**, because only the module world can see the real interface instance. Scope the `set` to the agent(s) that need it, using an absolute path with `null` context. Components fetch it in `build_phase`. A cleaner variant: the test gets it once and stores it in each agent's config object.

```mermaid
flowchart TD
  TOP["tb_top initial: config_db set(null, 'uvm_test_top.env.agt_a*', 'vif', a_if)"] --> RT["run_test()"]
  RT --> TEST["test build: get vif, put into agent_cfg"]
  TEST --> ENV["env build: set agent_cfg for agt_a"]
  ENV --> AGT["agent build: get cfg"]
  AGT --> DRV["driver/monitor: vif = cfg.vif"]
```

### Code
```systemverilog
